{
  /*
   * Types for the Edge Functions, which run on Deno — not Node, not a browser
   * tab. `Deno.serve` / `Deno.env` come with the runtime, so no tsconfig used to
   * claim these files and the editor's TypeScript server checked
   * `admin-create-user/index.ts` as a plain script: every `Deno` reference
   * reported TS2304 ("Cannot find name 'Deno'"), while `npm run build` in
   * `dashboard/` stayed silent because its tsconfig only includes `src`. Same
   * story as `dashboard/tsconfig.node.json`, and fixed the same way.
   *
   * `"types": ["deno"]` is what resolves those globals, exactly as
   * `"types": ["node"]` resolves `path` / `__dirname` over there: `@types/deno`
   * is the Deno authors' own `lib.deno*.d.ts`, republished on npm for an editor
   * with no Deno toolchain (and no Deno extension) installed. `lib` stays
   * DOM-shaped because the `Request`/`Response` a handler receives are the web
   * ones Deno implements.
   *
   * The other half is `npm-imports.d.ts`: Deno resolves the `npm:` specifier in
   * `index.ts` by itself, but a TypeScript server cannot, so that file names the
   * npm package it stands for. Both are dev-only — `supabase functions deploy`
   * bundles what a function imports, so nothing in this folder ships. Runs with
   * whatever TypeScript is on the machine; `npm install` here only pulls the
   * types.
   *
   * Check it with `npm install && npm run typecheck` from this folder.
   */
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "types": ["deno"],
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true
  },
  /*
   * Every function in this folder, plus the type declarations above them, so a
   * new `supabase/functions/<name>/index.ts` is covered the moment it is created.
   * `node_modules` is excluded by TypeScript's own default.
   */
  "include": ["**/*.ts"]
}
